I'm not sure that I understand sarcasm to be humor, hence the xo'o=20
similar to zo'o doesn't work for me.  Maybe parody is the boundary=20
between sarcasm and humor (but there are probably a few ways to mark parody=
.

I believe that, back when I analyzed attitudinal coverage, most forms of=20
sarcasm were to conveyed by making a statement and marking it with=20
.ianai or .ienai, to indicate that you don't really believe what you are=20
saying.  je'unai would have similar effect.  Depending on why you are=20
being sarcastic, .ionai might be added to one of the other choices=20
mentioned. (I suspect that is the usual reason why *I* express sarcasm)

Irony, which also overlaps sarcasm and humor, has the gismu ranxi=20
assigned, so rather than inventing a cmavo I would probably do "sei=20
ranxi [se'u]" to mark it.

